From 9227d7a00786b6444815c77abd6a299d7ab8c722 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AOSP RK3576 Baseline <uhf-platform@localbuild>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 10:14:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 02/15] uhf: drop the premature versions_with_info freeze
 declaration

Real build failure, found by actually running the build (not by inspection):

  error: hardware/rockchip/uhf/aidl/Android.bp:11:9: module
  "rockchip.uhf.aidl_interface": srcs: No sources for a previous version
  in aidl_api/rockchip.uhf.aidl/1. Was a version manually added to .bp
  file? This is added automatically by <module>-freeze-api.

The original Android.bp copied hwc_proxy_service's rockchip.hwc.proxy.aidl
versions_with_info: [{version: "1", ...}] block as a structural precedent,
but that module's version 1 only builds because its
aidl_api/rockchip.hwc.proxy.aidl/1/ snapshot was actually generated by
running <module>-freeze-api once that interface stabilized. Declaring a
frozen version without ever running the freeze step - which is what
happened here - is exactly the failure Soong's error message describes.

Fix: build rockchip.uhf.aidl against "current" (no versions_with_info),
which is correct for an interface still mid-development (UHF-SRS-001
Phase 2/3, not yet stabilized for a release). The VINTF manifest/matrix
fragments' <version>1</version> needs no change - an unfrozen "current"
AIDL interface is conventionally treated as version 1 for VINTF matching
until it's actually frozen via <module>-freeze-api, at which point that
freeze becomes version 1 for real.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 aidl/Android.bp | 16 ++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/aidl/Android.bp b/aidl/Android.bp
index cdcd025..a618403 100644
--- a/aidl/Android.bp
+++ b/aidl/Android.bp
@@ -23,10 +23,14 @@ aidl_interface {
             enabled: true,
         },
     },
-    versions_with_info: [
-        {
-            version: "1",
-            imports: [],
-        },
-    ],
+    // Deliberately unfrozen (no versions_with_info), unlike hwc_proxy_service's
+    // rockchip.hwc.proxy.aidl: that module's versions_with_info: [{version: "1", ...}] only builds
+    // because its aidl_api/rockchip.hwc.proxy.aidl/1/ snapshot was actually generated by running
+    // <module>-freeze-api once that interface stabilized. This interface is still mid-development
+    // (UHF-SRS-001 Phase 2/3), so it builds against "current" instead — declaring a frozen v1 here
+    // without ever running the freeze step is what breaks the build (confirmed: Soong requires the
+    // snapshot to exist on disk). The VINTF manifest/matrix fragments' <version>1</version> is still
+    // correct as-is: an unfrozen "current" AIDL interface is conventionally treated as version 1
+    // for VINTF matching purposes until it is actually frozen (`m rockchip.uhf.aidl-freeze-api`),
+    // at which point that freeze becomes version 1 for real and this comment should be removed.
 }
